.Dd July 29, 2026
.Dt LIBSHMRING 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm shmring_create ,
.Nm shmring_open ,
.Nm shmring_write ,
.Nm shmring_read ,
.Nm shmring_write_record ,
.Nm shmring_read_record
.Nd capability-safe shared-memory transport rings
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libshmring
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In shmring.h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
library creates bounded, unidirectional shared-memory rings for communication
between capability-mode processes.
Each ring is single-producer, single-consumer.
Callers with multiple producer or consumer threads must serialize access on
the corresponding side.
Each endpoint consists of separate immutable configuration, data,
producer-head, and consumer-tail descriptors.
Descriptor rights ensure that only the producer can modify data and the head,
and only the consumer can modify the tail.
.Pp
.Dv SHMRING_MODE_STREAM
provides a byte stream.
.Dv SHMRING_MODE_RECORD
preserves record boundaries and is suitable for datagrams and framed
component messages.
Capacities must be powers of two between
.Dv SHMRING_MIN_CAPACITY
and
.Dv SHMRING_MAX_CAPACITY .
.Pp
The library does not provide wakeups.
Users should send edge notifications over a kqueueable
.Xr libservice 3
channel after publishing data or freeing space.
.Pp
The
.Ql shmring
DTrace provider exposes creation, mapping, read, write, close, and invariant
violation probes.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cap_enter 2 ,
.Xr mmap 2 ,
.Xr libservice 3
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
All shared state is validated before use.
Object sizes and required memfd seals are checked before mappings are
dereferenced, so forged short or mutable objects fail with
.Er EPROTO
rather than generating a mapping fault.
A violated position or record invariant fails with
.Er EPROTO .
Callers should treat that error as a compromised peer and destroy the
component session.
